# This is an example service_bundle_contexts file that configures selected Service Bundles to have
# custom SELinux domains instead of the default untrusted_service_bundle domain.
# The service_bundle_contexts is not (yet) part of the standard Android SELinux configuration
# files, so it's kept separately and placed among other policy files.

# This imaginary firmware updater has its own SELinux domain, the firmware_updater, which allows
# additional permissions. The firmware_updater domain must be defined in regular Android SELinux
# policies, amond product policies, otherwise there is a runtime error when the Service Bundle is
# attempted to be executed.
# TODO: b/367205614 - use a real test bundle and define real test domain for it
com.sdv.oem.firmware.Updater      u:r:firmware_updater_bundle:s0

# This imaginary car update service also has its own SELinux domain.
# TODO: b/367205614 - use a real test bundle and define real test domain for it
com.sdv.oem.car.update.Service    u:r:car_update_service_bundle:s0
